<!--
    global.asa is NOT the same mechanism as the layout/#include pattern above,
    and it would NOT fix this feature request even though it's also
    "something every page implicitly gets."

    IIS looks for exactly one file named global.asa, in the site root, and
    runs specific subs in it in response to four lifecycle EVENTS — it is
    never #included or pasted into anything:

      Session_OnStart   - fires once per new user session
      Session_OnEnd     - fires once that session expires
      Application_OnStart - fires once when the app pool starts
      Application_OnEnd  - fires once when it shuts down

    Anything declared here (Session/Application variables, or objects
    stashed in them) IS visible from every page, but only as values sitting
    in the Session/Application collections at runtime — there is no source
    text from global.asa merged into view-order.asp the way _lib.DateTime.asp
    is. A "Go To Definition" on something set up in here would need to
    resolve a runtime dictionary lookup, not a text-inclusion chain, which is
    a different (and much harder) problem than what this feature request is
    actually asking for.
-->
<script language="VBScript" runat="server">
Sub Application_OnStart
    Application("SiteName") = "Acme Ordering"
End Sub

Sub Session_OnStart
    Session("CartCount") = 0
End Sub
</script>
